WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.440
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.440
<b>Noukin</b>

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:10.740
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.820
<i>Those eyes...</i>

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.950
<i>These are people who have put in the work!</i>

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:15.360
Kabaddi!

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.960
He turned a right angle 
without hitting the brakes?!

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.920
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.420
He's going under!

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.430
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.770
<i>A feint?!</i>

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.400
<i>That's why I will do the same!</i>

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.240
Kabaddi!

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.660
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.310
<i>Watch me.</i>

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.070
<i>Because I am... the ace!</i>

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.310
<i>The Direction
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWe're Aiming</i>

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.620
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.790
<b>Anti</b>

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.790
<b>Anti</b>

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:30.750
<i>In general, antis do not imagine 
themselves getting touched.</i>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:35.250
<i>Their aim is always one of two 
things—either dodge or catch.</i>

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:41.340
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:37.820
<i>However...</i>

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.930
<i>as Sakura approaches all of them, he has 
added in a slight touching movement.</i>

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.200
<i>And that movement suggests 
to the imagination that...</i>

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.130
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:47.780
They fell back!

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:54.200
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.120
I'm counting on you, guys.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.030
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.530
<b>Defense
Noukin 7 Players</b>

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.150
He's coming!

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.030
<b>Raider
Kouyou / Sakura</b>

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.030
Kabaddi.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.050
Kabaddi!

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.780
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.040
<i>I can't react at all!</i>

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.610
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.040
Push him back, Seki!

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:11.920
Blast it!

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.290
Kabaddi.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.040
<i>He's coming deeper?!</i>

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.670
He's aiming to get a huge number of points!

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.940
<i>I'm not letting you take the 
bonus that easily, Sakura!</i>

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:31.990
Kabaddi.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.280
Kabaddi!

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.080
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:43.720
<i>This is...!</i>

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.200
Senpai!

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.010
Kabaddi!

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.250
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.170
Through the defense?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.330
Three people in an instant?!

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.840
Kabaddi.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.880
No! We can't let him get back!

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.900
Sakura is strong, even after he makes a touch!

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:05.690
Kabaddi.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.970
A straight-ahead power battle?!

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:10.590
He's going over!

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:12.350
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.810
Kabaddi!

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.350
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.110
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.560
<i>You gave me a reason to seek to be stronger.</i>

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.520
<i>To live up to your expectations,</i>

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.220
<i>I've polished my skills and trained my body.</i>

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:33.270
<i>Every person I come into contact with...</i>

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:35.840
<i>is...</i>

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:38.470
<i>my strength!</i>

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.520
<i>If I go, I'll get touched!</i>

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.480
<i>Damn it! All we can do is shove him back!</i>

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:48.900
Kabaddi!

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.120
<i>It isn't enough yet!</i>

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.490
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.020
<i>Huh?</i>

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.530
<i>Right...</i>

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:58.620
<i>Hiro?</i>

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.840
When the time comes that 
you really want to win...

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:08.650
you won't lose to anyone.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.960
That's what I think, anyway.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:17.020
K-Kouyou, one point from the 
bonus, and from touches...

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:18.050
Six points!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.250
All right! Yeah!

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.060
That's seven points!

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.760
I've never seen anything like that!

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.210
That greed, at the end there, wasn't like you.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.790
Yeah. I have this terrible friend, you see.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.190
He's always saying to me...

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:46.380
"You're the most amazing athlete 
out there. You can do more."

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.510
What an irresponsible guy!

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:51.980
Right?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.160
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.160
<b>Noukin</b>

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.020
<i>The monster that gained 
seven points in one turn</i>

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.170
<i>didn't make a pose of triumph.</i>

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.450
<i>He didn't smile.</i>

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.180
<i>Instead, he bowed deeply</i>

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.010
<i>in a posture of profound gratitude.</i>

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.390
Seven points in a single raid?

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:23.160
After this, even in the future, 
we may never see anything like it again.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.440
That was not a normal play.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.060
Yoigoshi-kun...

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.160
Mentally, this must be rough on him.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:34.580
<i>That's right. He was the 
only one I couldn't reel in.</i>

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:38.710
<i>If this made him shrink back a bit,
 that would be ideal, but...</i>

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.710
<i>he is "Yoigoshi the Unstoppable," after all.</i>

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.860
<i>Gratitude, huh? What a nuisance.</i>

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:50.730
<i>He did a stupid amount of training,</i>

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.980
<i>and made it through in the 
spirit of repaying a kindness.</i>

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:56.440
<i>That's a way of thinking I don't possess.</i>

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.480
<i>It isn't logical, but...</i>

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:01.350
<i>if you've got game sense, it's different.</i>

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.550
<i>What looks like pointless 
training at first glance,</i>

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.360
<i>can become something meaningful.</i>

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.240
<i>He really is a nuisance.</i>

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.360
<i>And for precisely that reason...</i>

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.530
<i>I have to crush him!</i>

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.120
<b>Defense
Kouyou 7 Players</b>

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.120
<b>Raider
Noukin / Yoigoshi</b>

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:17.990
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.000
Kabaddi!

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.880
Damn it. That freakin' berserker!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.630
<i>We're not letting you take out Sakura!</i>

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.750
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:27.400
Kabaddi!

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.130
He's targeting Sakura again!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:34.110
I get why he's all worked up, 
since they're both raiders, but...

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:37.640
If we want to get back on our feet here, 
the only option is to drive Sakura out.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:41.270
Besides, something about Sakura seems off.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:45.810
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:49.320
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:55.230
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:51.720
<i>He isn't moving badly, but...</i>

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.230
<i>he's only thinking about evading. 
He's not in position for a catch!</i>

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.580
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.580
<i>This is my chance to drive Sakura out!</i>

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.700
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.310
All the way in the back?!

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:10.570
That technique is...

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:12.300
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:15.550
Kabaddi!

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.430
Kabaddi!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.060
<i>That was close!</i>

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:22.940
<i>What?!</i>

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:25.160
<i>Sakura!</i>

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.440
<i>I must give thanks once more.</i>

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.990
Noukin, raid failed! Lona!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:46.790
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:46.790
<b>Noukin</b>

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:44.780
Kouyou gains three points!

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:46.790
That means...

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.290
We made a comeback!

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:50.500
Yay!

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:52.280
Thank you!

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.690
What are you talking about?

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:56.820
That was your strength, right, 
Sakura? The seven-point man.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:08:59.810
Yeah.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:02.790
Let's win this!

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:05.840
Leave it to me.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:10.940
I'm... very sorry.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.050
Y-Yoigoshi?

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:21.540
<i>Noukin starts again with a seven-man defense.</i>

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:26.900
<i>Wary of Sakura, they try to prevent 
another high scoring round.</i>

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.210
Kabaddi.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.240
Kabaddi!

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.930
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.060
Nice one, Sakura!

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.430
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.430
<b>Noukin</b>

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.460
End of the first half! Halftime!

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:49.240
We're four points... behind.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.680
Yoigoshi-kun, your drink.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:56.460
I'm fine.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:05.320
It's hot.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:07.200
That's cold!

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.080
Captain?!

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.960
I froze the bottles.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.690
You need to rehydrate. 
There's still the second half, after all.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:17.940
The second half...

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:22.730
Failing a raid is something 
that happens a lot.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:24.480
If you let it get to you, 
there'll be no end to it.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.150
I know that.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.730
But this time was different. 
The direction was...

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.380
The direction?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.980
Everybody practices for the 
purpose of winning games.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.450
The time spent on teams looks 
pretty much the same everywhere.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.750
The way people grow depends on talent,

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:46.750
but the thing that makes the most 
difference is... the nature of the effort.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.960
It's important to know if the 
direction you're aiming is right or not.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:55.160
If all you're doing is sweating, 
anyone can do that.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:58.280
You think like a coach.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:10:59.880
All this time...

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.260
I've been practicing that.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.140
The direction I'm aiming...

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.180
Maybe I went wrong somewhere.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.150
It's fine, though.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.830
I'm not that weak.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:20.330
I just wasted some time, that's all.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:21.610
I can get it back.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:25.290
Your legs... Is there 
anything wrong with them?

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:26.390
My legs?

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.790
Nothing's wrong.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:33.100
Changing directions puts more strain 
on them than you realize.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:38.300
In kabaddi, you have to change 
directions quickly on a small court.

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:41.870
As long as your territory's behind you, 
if you can do a quick back,

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.930
it will become a supreme raiding technique.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.430
What are you trying to say?

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.440
I thought the same, a long time ago.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:54.060
The skill you used, Back, 
it's something I was aiming for, too.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:58.350
Why... Why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:01.210
If I'd started practicing it sooner, 
it would have been closer to complete!

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:05.280
I already told you. It inflicts 
a huge amount of strain.

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:08.300
W-Was the reason you were hospitalized...

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:09.170
That's right.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.160
I never thought I'd go down first.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:16.470
You have an inherent knack for shifting 
your weight, adjusting your stride,

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:19.330
and national-level feinting skills.

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:23.480
Plus, intuition honed through soccer.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:25.930
You probably won't break so easily.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.350
But a failure is a failure.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:32.780
I have no intention of saying 
"you're so close" to comfort you.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:34.690
You wouldn't accept it anyway, right?

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:36.810
So...

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.660
all I can say is this...

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:42.400
Hey, Yoigoshi-kun.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.630
Was I wrong in aiming to acquire that skill?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.660
You weren't wrong.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.330
Right?

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.200
That's all.

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.660
Well, I'll head back.

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:05.180
<i>The direction I'm aiming...</i>

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.100
<i>Ever since that day...</i>

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:09.810
<i>the direction I've been aiming is...</i>

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.230
I see.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.150
I did have...

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.280
That's true.

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:32.990
In soccer, he was recognized as 
an athlete at the national level.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:35.240
Still, I...

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:36.760
won't be beaten.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:47.180
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:47.180
<b>Noukin</b>

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.410
This starts the second half! 
The raid goes to Noukin!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.240
<b>Raider
Noukin / Yoigoshi</b>

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:53.530
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:54.930
<b>Defense
Noukin 7 Players</b>

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.880
Stop him! We're going to 
keep this up and pull away!

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:54.930
Sir!

00:13:54.930 --> 00:14:00.670
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:02.570
Kabaddi.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.020
Kabaddi!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:05.480
Kabaddi.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.300
Kabaddi!

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:10.930
<i>Which will he use?</i>

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.660
<i>That super-sharp Cut?</i>

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:15.240
<i>Or a Back?</i>

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:31.300
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.220
<i>He just failed at using the Back.</i>

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.840
<i>This isn't his only chance to try it again.</i>

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:26.410
It'll be the Back.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:29.800
<i>Will it be the Cut?</i>

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.220
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.220
<i>How will he come at us?</i>

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:37.810
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:41.810
<i>I...</i>

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.160
They're flanking him!

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.270
They're anticipating a Cut!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.100
<i>The direction I'm aiming...</i>

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.380
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:54.660
It was a Back!

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.190
Yeah.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:14:59.920
<i>What?!</i>

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.200
It can't be!

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.170
They caught up?!

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:04.510
<i>Flanking was just the run-up!</i>

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:07.420
<i>If we started at the same time
 as you we'll never catch up!</i>

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:10.120
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:15.850
Kabaddi!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:25.020
Kabaddi!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.480
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.330
He blasted through the 
defense and made it back!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.450
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.450
<b>Noukin</b>

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:37.180
Noukin, three points by touch!

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.040
He got those back in a flash!

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:45.720
Man! Even when we predict right,
 this is how it turns out?

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:51.970
That was great! You succeeded!

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.330
That was a failure.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:56.790
Huh? Why?

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.380
You made it back, right?

00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:03.410
No. It was only by chance that I was 
in a position to knock out the enemy.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:08.230
<i>Back isn't a skill used to 
get a huge number of points.</i>

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.650
<i>Barely making contact with the 
enemy is the merit of the skill,</i>

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.980
<i>and what determines its success.</i>

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.340
<i>I can see why the captain</i>

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:19.320
<i>with his lack of physical strength 
tried to learn this skill,</i>

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:25.090
<i>but I have the speed and 
weight to repel the enemy.</i>

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:30.660
<i>The skill itself was unfinished 
and as yet unsuccessful,</i>

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.560
<i>but a slim possibility had been 
uncovered just by chance.</i>

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:39.100
<i>And, there was a sense of growth 
he'd felt many times in the past.</i>

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.890
<i>With this skill...</i>

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.140
<i>I will surpass the captain!</i>

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:52.030
<b>Defense
Noukin 7 Players</b>

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:50.990
Let's keep up the momentum!

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.030
Sir!

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:56.030
<b>Raider
Kouyou / Sakura</b>

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:57.450
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:01.950
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.550
<i>The defense has fallen back?</i>

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:01.950
<i>Are they prioritizing evasion?</i>

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:10.000
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:08.860
<i>Everyone's just supposed 
to be menacing him...</i>

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:10.800
<i>but I'm going in to challenge him!</i>

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:16.510
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.010
<i>The second he shows me an opening!</i>

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:17.940
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.140
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:25.850
Kouyou, two points gained!

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:28.610
<i>You can't be serious!</i>

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.780
<i>I couldn't even challenge him!</i>

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.820
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.820
<b>Noukin</b>

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:35.130
<i>And so the match continued.</i>

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:38.820
<i>Yoigoshi fought bravely,</i>

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.830
<i>but the point gap did not close.</i>

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.080
<i>As both teams...</i>

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:46.310
<i>approached their peak fatigue...</i>

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:50.330
<i>they could no longer move well 
enough to execute their plans.</i>

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.470
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.470
<b>Noukin</b>

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.940
Noukin, time out!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:07.240
<i>They could not defend against 
Sakura's fierce attacks,</i>

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:08.790
<i>and it ate away not just 
at their physical strength,</i>

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:10.950
<i>but their mental strength, as well.</i>

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.390
Seki, you're switching out.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.560
Thank you. You bought enough time 
for my bleeding to stop.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.750
No. I'm very sorry.

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:24.700
All I did out there was get touched.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.740
It's your first match. 
Don't let it bother you.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:32.090
But, after entering and exiting 
the court over and over...

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.740
I started thinking it might 
be better if I wasn't there.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.890
Over and over again...

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:43.390
It was like I went back just 
to have points taken from me.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:49.000
I started thinking that it would 
be better if I wasn't there.

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:51.770
Hey!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:53.510
Huh?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:54.200
Misumi!

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:56.640
Oh. Sorry.

00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:58.890
Kyohei...

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:05.290
<i>You can tell Sakura's an amazing 
player just by looking at him.</i>

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.040
<i>I don't even know how many 
times he's gotten me.</i>

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:11.020
<i>But I won't ever accept it!</i>

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:16.450
<i>"It'd be better if I wasn't here." 
I'll never say anything so uncool!</i>

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:22.410
I am #3, a striker! A Noukin anti!

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:26.300
I'm #1, a striker! And a raider!

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:27.350
Masato?!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:28.700
That's no fair!

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:31.150
"Striker" feels better than "Backup," 
like a nice ground ball.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:33.480
I'm both, though...

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.360
Nobody cares!

00:19:38.270 --> 00:19:39.600
<i>The tension is gone.</i>

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.570
Play resumes!

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:47.580
<b>Defense
Noukin 6 Players</b>

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.430
<i>We'll win this!</i>

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.080
<b>Raider
Kouyou / Sakura</b>

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:51.400
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:52.580
<i>We won't let you beat us!</i>

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.590
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.590
<b>Noukin</b>

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:55.160
<i>A minute and a half left...</i>

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:58.620
<i>We're trailing by two points...</i>

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.160
<i>and I still haven't been able 
to put up a decent fight!</i>

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:03.730
In the second half,

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:06.850
we'll continue to feign focusing on 
a catch and aim to wear Sakura out.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.630
Because he has explosive 
powers of concentration,

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.600
the fatigue must be just as extreme.

00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:16.860
<i>Sakura will target the captain until he 
sees an opening among the rest of us.</i>

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:18.890
Kabaddi...

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:20.910
Kabaddi...

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.300
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.930
<i>I don't know anything about this sense of 
rivalry towards a master teacher,</i>

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:32.810
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:32.810
<i>but I'll use that to challenge him on this turn.</i>

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:35.970
<i>Don't rush things, Misumi.</i>

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:38.380
<i>Wait until Sakura comes deeper.</i>

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:45.880
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:40.150
<i>That's why we've all fallen back!</i>

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.340
<i>Coupled with the fact that 
I never went for a catch,</i>

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:47.180
<i>he must have the impression 
that we're focused on evasion.</i>

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:51.680
<i>The only time I'll actually be able 
to catch him is when he's wide open.</i>

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:50.240
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.710
<i>Find it... the perfect timing...</i>

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.400
<i>the opening...</i>

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.190
<i>And with everything I've got...</i>

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:02.190
<i>And with everything I've got...</i>

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:07.950
<i>A difference in experience.</i>

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:11.510
<i>To target when one appears 
not to be targeting.</i>

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:15.400
<i>In kabaddi, this is an everyday occurrence.</i>

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:16.830
<i>In short,</i>

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:20.640
<i>there wasn't a trace of an opening to 
take advantage of in the first place.</i>

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:22.670
The captain!

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.590
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:28.410
Not good!

00:21:29.690 --> 00:21:30.660
I've got nowhere to run!

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.670
Kabaddi!

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:36.570
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:53.050
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:47.770
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:49.370
<i>Stop right there, you jerk!</i>

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:52.700
<i>I will be useful to the captain, to the team!</i>

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:54.520
Kabaddi!

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:08.560
Kouyou, three points gained!

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:18.980
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:18.980
<b>Noukin</b>

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"After Giving Every Last Drop"</b>

00:23:49.310 --> 00:23:52.480
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:49.720 --> 00:23:52.860
Next time, "After Giving Every Last Drop!"

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:53.190
Kabaddi!
